#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "okta.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To Okta Partner Group Integration
	Testing to assure koroneiki partner and group integration to okta works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
    * I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | okt.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OKT                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| OKTKOROKTKOR |
	| OKTPAROKTPAR |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Oktkor - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| OKTKOROKTKOR |
	| OKTPAROKTPAR |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| okt.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| okt.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| okt.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| okt.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| okt.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| okt.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Oktkor - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Sync partner group membership via koroneiki to okta
	Koroneiki partner contacts with the proper group synced via Koroneiki should be properly synced to okta.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Name   | Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Code   | OKTPAROKTPAR                  | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Member |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned to the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | OKTKOROKTKOR                     | |
	| Language                   | English                          | |
	| Name                       | Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	And I assign the team with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign the team with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I create a postal address for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Main Street |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	Then the support organization with the code "OKTPAROKTPAR" should be part of the support site
	And the user with the email address "okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be a member of the okta group "Partners"
	And the koroneiki contact and the okta user with the email address "okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should have matching uuid values

Scenario: Sync partner user updates to okta
	Koroneiki partner contacts with subsequent updates made via Koroneiki and synced via Provisioning should be properly synced to okta.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Name   | Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Code   | OKTPAROKTPAR                  | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Member |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned to the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | OKTKOROKTKOR                     | |
	| Language                   | English                          | |
	| Name                       | Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	And I assign the team with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign the team with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I create a postal address for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Main Street |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	Then the support organization with the code "OKTPAROKTPAR" should be part of the support site
	And the user with the email address "okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be a member of the okta group "Partners"
	When I update a koroneiki contact with the email address "okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to have the following values
	| Email Address | okt.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OKT                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner2                          |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "okt.partner2"
	And I click on the user with the name "OKT Partner2" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the sync with okta button in the user details page
	# Necessary pause for Partners to sync correctly
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	Then the user with the email address "okt.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on okta
	And the koroneiki contact and the okta user with the email address "okt.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should have matching uuid values

Scenario: Sync partner group membership via provisioning to okta
	Koroneiki partner contacts with the proper group synced via Provisioning should be properly synced to okta.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Name   | Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Code   | OKTPAROKTPAR                  | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned to the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | OKTKOROKTKOR                     | |
	| Language                   | English                          | |
	| Name                       | Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	And I assign the team with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign the team with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I create a postal address for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Main Street |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	Then the support organization with the code "OKTPAROKTPAR" should be part of the support site
	When I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Oktpar"
	And I click on the account with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	And I click on the assign contact button
	And I populate and save the assign contact form with the following values
	| Email Address | okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| Assign Role   | Partner Member                    |
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | OKT Partner1                      |
	| Email Address | okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| Role          | Partner Member                    |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                          |
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "okt.partner1"
	And I click on the user with the name "OKT Partner1" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the sync with okta button in the user details page
	# Necessary pause for Partners to sync correctly
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	Then the user with the email address "okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be a member of the okta group "Partners"
	And the koroneiki contact and the okta user with the email address "okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should have matching uuid values

Scenario: Sync partner group membership removal via koroneiki to okta
	Koroneiki partner contacts with the proper group synced via Koroneiki should be properly synced to okta.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Name   | Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Code   | OKTPAROKTPAR                  | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "okt.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Oktpar - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Member |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
